```php
final class OffPeakWindow
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly int $startSeconds, // inclusive
        private readonly int $endSeconds,   // exclusive
        private readonly string $multiplier,
    ) {
        if ($startSeconds < 0 || $startSeconds >= 86400) throw ValueError
        ...
        assertDecimal(multiplier)? multiplier is already validated at parse time; keep it light here.
    }

    public static function parse(string $windowStart, string $windowEnd, string $multiplier): self
    {
        return new self(self::parseTimeOfDay($windowStart, 'window_start'), self::parseTimeOfDay($windowEnd, 'window_end'), $multiplier);
    }

    /** HH:MM → seconds within a day. */
    public static function parseTimeOfDay(string $value, string $field): int
    {
        if (preg_match('/^(\d{1,2}):(\d{2})$/', $value) !== 1) {
            throw new ValueError("$field: ожидалось время в формате ЧЧ:ММ, получено: " . $value);
        }
        $h = (int) $m[1]; $min = (int) $m[2];
        if ($h > 23 || $min > 59) throw new ValueError(...);
        return $h * 3600 + $min * 60;
    }

    public function multiplier(): string { return $this->multiplier; }

    /**
     * Whether a given UTC moment falls within the [start, end) window (the window may cross midnight).
     * If start == end the window is empty (no discount).
     */
    public function covers(\DateTimeInterface $utc): bool
    {
        $t = (int) $utc->format('G'); // G = seconds since midnight
        if ($this->startSeconds === $this->endSeconds) {
            return false;
        }
        if ($this->startSeconds < $this->endSeconds) {
            return $t >= $this->startSeconds && $t < $this->endSeconds;
        }
        return $t >= $this->startSeconds || $t < $this->endSeconds;
    }
}
```

Wait, `format('G')` returns a string; (int) will do it. G = "second from midnight (seconds from midnight)" — yes, e.g. "39600" for 11:00:00.

